Online office WOPI host for Tryton
==================================

This module exposes a WOPI host for one binary field of one Tryton record.
It does not expose a file system, and consequently deliberately does not claim
support for relative-file operations.  `DeleteFile` clears the binary field.
`RenameFile` is available only if the binary field declares `filename`; it
updates that filename field and retains its extension.

Configuration
-------------

Add the following server configuration. ``[office] url`` is the only online
office setting; it can point to either Collabora Online or ONLYOFFICE Docs.
``[wopi] url`` must be reachable by that office server::

    [office]
    url = https://office.example.com
    discovery_timeout = 10

    [wopi]
    url = https://tryton.example.com
    secret = a-random-secret-with-at-least-32-bytes
    lease_time = 1800
    require_proof = true

The ``[wopi]`` section contains the WOPI URL reachable by the online office,
the secret and the lease time. The browser launch URL is built from
``[web] base_url``. This allows a local browser to use ``localhost`` while a
containerized online office uses a host-gateway address for WOPI callbacks.
The module reads the configured server's WOPI discovery document to obtain its
supported edit actions. It does not require a provider setting.
When the discovery document includes ``proof-key``, the module requires and
validates ``X-WOPI-Proof``, ``X-WOPI-ProofOld`` and ``X-WOPI-TimeStamp`` on
every WOPI callback. Keep ``require_proof`` enabled in production. A Collabora
installation that does not publish proof keys can set it to ``false`` as an
explicit compatibility exception, but then network access to the WOPI routes
must be restricted to the office server.

`[wopi] secret` must be stored in the server configuration or a secret
manager, never in the database.  Restrict the reverse proxy so only the
configured online office can call `/<database>/wopi/`; TLS is mandatory in
production.

`lease_time` is the number of seconds that an inactive editor session remains
valid.  Every authenticated WOPI request renews the lease.  For compatibility,
the old `token_lifetime` setting is used as a fallback when `lease_time` is not
set.

If `[wopi] url` is not set, the module uses the first non-empty origin
configured in `[web] cors` (or `TRYTOND_WEB__CORS`).  Set `[wopi] url`
explicitly when the CORS list contains more than one origin or its first value
is not Tryton's public URL.

Opening an editor
-----------------

Open this authenticated Tryton URL in a new browser tab::

    /<database>/wopi/open/<model>/<record>/<binary-field>?name=<filename>

The previous ``/collabora/open`` launch path remains available as a
compatibility alias.

The endpoint checks model, field and record rules, reads the selected office's
discovery document and posts to its versioned edit action.  It creates a short-lived,
HMAC-signed capability for exactly that binary field; the browser user never
supplies credentials to Collabora.

The reusable `wopi.editor.get_editor_url()` function returns this
launch URL.  The module also adds an `Open` button to `ir.attachment`; it
returns an `ir.action.url`, which clients open in a new browser tab, and is
shown only for editable formats published by the configured office server.

The host implements CheckFileInfo, GetFile, PutFile, DeleteFile, RenameFile
(where applicable), Lock, GetLock, RefreshLock, Unlock and UnlockAndRelock.
All users opening the same record and binary field share a stable WOPI file
identifier, which lets the selected office place them in the same co-authoring session.
Each user still has an independent signed access token and lease.
Permissions are rechecked on every WOPI callback, so a revoked Tryton
permission immediately stops access.
